  "result": "The fix is in. Shell completion no longer drops the rest of the command line after an argument containing `#`. The full test suite passes (1909 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n**Change:** In `split_arg_string` (`src/click/shell_completion.py`), I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is treated as an ordinary character. Before the fix, `cli a #b c` split to `[\"cli\", \"a\"]`. This function is shared by all four shells, so the fix covers bash, zsh, fish and PowerShell.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `tests/test_parser.py`: added `cli a #b c` and `cli a#b`. Both fail without the fix and pass with it.\n- `tests/test_shell_completion.py`: added a bash end-to-end case, `COMP_WORDS=\"a #\"`. Its expected output is a bare newline, which is what the bash path prints when nothing matches. I set the expectation to match that existing behavior.\n\n**Changelog:** `CHANGES.md` has a new \"Unreleased\" section above 8.5.0.\n\nI haven't committed anything. Say the word if you want a commit.",
